/-!
# B-line machine, sweep 3: the `B₀` axis map as seven passes

On a `(pre, N, post)` array of Gaussian items (`N = n_c λ`), the in-place `B₀` line map of the
axis (`axisL N post (lineB …)`) is computed by (`axisPipe`):

1. a selection slab pass (row `rowSel l`, scaled by `2^{P-p-1}`, zeros for `l ≥ s`);
2. the chunk kernel `chunkK` on every `λ`-chunk (one `λ`-exposure);
3. a slab gather of the `m` near-boundary rows `LJ` (padded to `G` rows);
4. the `J` kernel (`fwdK`, `bwdK`, coupling window) on every `G`-row (one `G`-exposure);
5. a slab scatter back to the `N` rows;
6. the chunk kernel again;
7. the output slab pass on the pair `(Y, Y₂)`: `outE l (Y - Y₂)`.

Real and imaginary parts are carried together (`liftG`). **`axisPipe_eq`** proves the equality.
-/

